# Cloudflare Workers static asset exclusions
.git/
node_modules/
data/ppp_sentences_en.db
data/ppp_concepts_en.db
data/ppp_transcripts_html_ru.db
data/ppp_lecture_extras.json
data/ppp_transcripts_html_lv.db
data/ppp_transcripts_html_en.db
data/ppp_meta.db

# 2026-08-24: the compressed sentence core crossed the 25 MiB Worker asset
# limit (13.7 -> 35.2 MiB) when the EN premium rebuild grew the sentence DB
# from ~677 to 1828 lectures. NOTHING fetches it from the Worker: the app's
# search reads the SHARDS (data/shards/*.db.br), and the offline installer's
# CORE_KEYS = ['meta','extras'] (js/downloader.js:34) dropped 'sentences' on
# 2026-07-27. The file stays in git / GitHub Pages; it is only excluded from
# the Worker asset upload, where its size is a hard deploy blocker.
data/ppp_sentences_en.db.br
data/ppp_sentences_en.db.gz
# 2026-08-25: the file is no longer built into deploy/ at all (dropped from the publish chain) — these two lines are now a dormant guard.

# transcripts served from GitHub Pages own-origin since phase2 (2026-07-31); not needed on Worker
transcripts/

# UNCOMPRESSED shard intermediates. build_sentence_shards.py writes a ~26 MB raw
# SQLite per shard before compressing it; on 2026-08-22 a killed step 8a2 left
# deploy/data/shards/ppp_sentences_shard_018.db (29.4 MiB) behind, and because
# wrangler uploads deploy/ FROM DISK (not from git) the next `wrangler deploy`
# died with rc=1 — Workers rejects any asset over 25 MiB, and the error never
# reached the log. The builder now writes those intermediates outside deploy/,
# so this line is the second, independent guard.
# NB: ONLY the raw .db — the published shards are .db.br / .db.gz, they are
# referenced by data/shards_manifest.json and MUST stay uploaded.
data/shards/*.db
